{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The exceptions in item (ii) attach locally to its removal and operate disjunctively.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The transition preserves the processing of specified applications without expressly adding a substantive exception to item (ii).","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Substantive qualification alone does not authorise an applicant to bypass the preserved process.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.8eb374ffa546ddd2ba291e37.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The specific Effective Date and the parent's fund, change and factual definitions are retained.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.6c6f3d526cc54d9f91476d290e5fda00","controlled_language":"The transition can be read as governing existing application processing only, while item (ii) independently states substantive relief conditions. On that reading, legacy application history does not itself negate substantive qualification, but the supplied text cannot determine whether the applicant may implement the change without prior approval. The selected control—actual availability of item (ii) relief for that application—remains unformalized because the necessary connecting authority is missing.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"SHARED_RESOLUTION","issue_ids":["issue.e51651909bfb44379b8c472604cbab84","issue.1e88c511e4d04cf0b2c2296dcca96e60","issue.6df93a480d9645db8f52d1a32b5c26ab","issue.c5d6feeb19bb46b4a808d10a2bbfb312"],"parent_id":"candidate.6a5b6dca04aa42a48ef7825c236dea80","probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"For a substantively qualifying change with a pending pre-Effective-Date application, reading_1 returns false for relief eligibility. This reading instead establishes substantive qualification and preserved processing separately, leaving actual relief availability unresolved. It therefore does not delete the legacy condition and return true for the same control. The strongest uncertainty is the absent rule connecting preserved processing to the continuing approval obligation. The rival is interpretively meaningful but is not a complete competing executable approval rule. A broader attachment of item (ii)'s exceptions to operator changes or notification alignment was tested and rejected as insufficiently supported by the separately numbered provisions.","run_id":"run.319c058876aa4441a4b41af39001d48a","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"6c557525c251e4c0794c0061ba5b7f7fec9be45d9495dd1ca07063f018b43c06","source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069","d97b56331f41a.u4.653","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Approval-relief eligibility with transition attached only to application processing"}